{
  "name": "combined_pairwise_loss",
  "intuition": "This crossover synergistically blends the smooth margin-based advantage gap loss with the rank-weighted softened margin loss to leverage the advantages of both approaches. The core idea is to use the stability and smoothness from the tanh-based transformation combined with dynamic rank weighting, ensuring the loss remains numerically stable and semantically meaningful. By merging the benefit of a smooth hinge-like behavior with adaptive weighting, this loss aims to improve robustness, gradient stability, and prioritization of informative pairs, addressing prior issues like instability or overfitting.",
  "pseudocode": "rank_weight = clamp(1.0 + gamma * delta_rank, 0.1, 10.0)\nmargin = ops.sub(lpw, lpl)\n\ndisturbed_margin = ops.sub(ops.mul(alpha, margin), ops.mul(beta, advantage_gap))\nx_tanh = ops.tanh(disturbed_margin)\nordinary_loss = ops.neg(ops.logsigmoid(x_tanh))\nweighted_loss = ops.mul( ops.mul(ordinary_loss, weight), ops.pow(rank_weight, 2.0) )\nnorm = ops.sum( ops.mul( weight, ops.pow(rank_weight, 2.0) ) ) + eps\nloss = ops.div( ops.sum(weighted_loss), norm )\nreturn loss",
